```json
{
  "candidates": [
    {"id": "find:find-remove:r1:F1", "verdict": "confirmed", "evidence": "SPEC.md line 3: '`Ledger.remove(sku, qty)`: raise `ValueError` if `qty` exceeds current stock.' vs stock.py lines 22-24: 'def remove(self, sku: str, qty: int) -> None:\\n    item = self.items[sku]\\n    item.qty -= qty' — no check or ValueError raised; qty is unconditionally subtracted, allowing item.qty to go negative."},
    {"id": "find:find-lowstock:r1:F1", "verdict": "confirmed", "evidence": "SPEC.md line 4: '`Ledger.low_stock(threshold)`: SKUs with `qty <= threshold`.' vs stock.py line 30: 'return [i.sku for i in self.items.values() if i.qty < threshold]' — uses strict '<' instead of '<=', so an item with qty exactly equal to threshold is excluded from the result."}
  ]
}
```

